LEE-YANG CIRCLE CHECK (W6): rim roots solve (q−2)^5 = −1 ⟹ |q−2| = 1
   q = +0.00000+0.00000i   |q−2| = 2.00000   [q=0/center]
   q = +1.00000+0.00000i   |q−2| = 1.00000   [ON |q−2|=1]
   q = +1.69098-0.95106i   |q−2| = 1.00000   [ON |q−2|=1]
   q = +1.69098+0.95106i   |q−2| = 1.00000   [ON |q−2|=1]
   q = +2.00000+0.00000i   |q−2| = 0.00000   [q=0/center]
   q = +2.80902-0.58779i   |q−2| = 1.00000   [ON |q−2|=1]
   q = +2.80902+0.58779i   |q−2| = 1.00000   [ON |q−2|=1]
   ⟹ the 5 rim roots lie exactly on the circle |q−2|=1; the real one (q=1) is where
     the Lee-Yang locus meets the real axis below χ=3. The HN gadget's zeros are circular.

